* bench.id: rob_hs_ff_utf16_le_with_bom
* bench.group: robustness
* bench.title: a valid 5 V divider saved as UTF-16 LE with a byte-order mark
* bench.expect: loud_error
* bench.tags: hostile, file, encoding
* bench.est_rss_mib: 64
* bench.note: neither tool reads UTF-16 text (ngspice-47 exits 0 without a rawfile, RustSpice refuses the invalid UTF-8): a loud refusal is correct, silent numbers would be a defect
